  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b>Your job</b>

    Users send a ticket when their PC has a problem.
    Fix every PC before too many users are lost.


    <b>Connecting</b>

    Click
    a ticket in the list to connect to that PC. Connecting takes a few seconds, and
    you can only work on one PC at a time. Disconnect with the button above the list.


    <b>The
    list goes stale</b>

    While you are connecting or connected, the other tickets
    stop updating: they are dimmed and only show what you last saw. When a PC you
    can''t see takes damage, you hear a beep and its ticket flashes red. Disconnect
    to see every ticket live again.


    <b>Rounds</b>

    Each PC is fixed by
    finishing its minigame a few times. The list and the minigame panel show which
    round you are on. Finished rounds stay finished when you leave.


    <b>Pressure</b>

    While
    a round is unsolved, the PC''s pressure meter fills, also while you are working
    on another PC. When it is full, the PC takes damage and the meter drops back
    to half. Finishing a round empties it.


    <b>Damage</b>

    Fine, Slightly
    broken, More broken, Blackout. At Blackout the user is lost and the ticket closes.
    The level ends when every ticket is closed, or when too many users are lost (see
    Game data).'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_fontSharedMaterials: []
  m_fontMaterial: {fileID: 0}
